              "feedback": {
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Iron refinement in the blast furnace example relies on density to separate the species produced by the reactions occurring at high temperatures in the furnace. The gas phase products (CO, CO"
                      },
                      {
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "2"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ") rise to the top of the furnace and are vented, while the molten liquids (Fe metal and CaSiO"
                      },
                      {
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "3"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": ", slag) flow to the bottom of the furnace. Since CaSiO"
                      },
                      {
                        "sub": true,
                        "text": "3"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " is less dense than iron metal, these liquid layers can be separated by their density as well."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1933674128",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
